    "knowledge_point": "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations Using Elimination",
    "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}v-2w=5 \\\\ -v-\\frac{2}{5}w=5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}v-2w=5 & |\\times 3 \\\\ -v-\\frac{2}{5}w=5 & |\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}5v-6w=15 \\\\ -5v-2w=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $v$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{5v}-6w & =15 \\\\ -\\cancel{5v}-2w & =25 \\\\ (-6w-2w) & =(15+25) \\\\ -8w & =40 \\\\ w & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $w=-5$ into the first equation to solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-6w & =15 \\\\ 5v-6(-5) & =15 \\\\ 5v+30 & =15 \\\\ 5v & =-15 \\\\ v & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $v=-3,\\,w=-5.$",
